@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Audiobook recommendations — system overview
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 180

actor User
package "recommenderagent — live requests" {
  component "RequestGateway\nCoordinates the request" as Gateway #DBEAFE
  component "InputParser\nCommand fast path OR AI intent extraction" as Parser #DBEAFE
  component "SessionTransitionService\nOwns session transaction" as Session #DBEAFE
  component "ConversationEngine + intent handlers\nResolve, validate and page" as Engine #DBEAFE
  component "AudiobookRecommendationWorkflow\nBuilds a new recommendation batch" as Workflow #DCFCE7
  component "CandidateRetrievalService\nDispatches ordered search strategies" as Retrieval #DCFCE7
  component "RankingService\nCombines weighted scorers\nRanks up to 20 recommendations" as Ranking #DCFCE7
  component "ConversationResponseGenerator\nFixed replies or AI narration" as Response #DBEAFE
  component "User preference adapter\nQdrant OR Solr" as UserAdapter #FEF3C7
  component "SessionRepository adapter\nCurrent runtime: Redis" as SessionStore #FEF3C7
}
component "shared.audiobookcatalogue\nAudiobook adapter: Qdrant OR Solr" as Adapter #FEF3C7
component "shared.readhistory\nReadHistoryRepository\nPostgreSQL or client adapter" as ReadHistory #FEF3C7
database "Selected database\nQdrant OR Solr\nCatalogue + book vectors\nUser preference vectors" as Qdrant
database "Redis\nSaved preferences + count\nSearch context + last outcome\nPending recommendations + shown IDs" as Redis
database "Read-history database\nUser/book pairs; separate from sessions" as HistoryDatabase

User -right-> Gateway : request / response
Gateway --> Parser : 1. Parse
Gateway --> Session : 2. Apply session transition
Session --> SessionStore : lock / load / commit / release
SessionStore --> Redis
Session --> Engine : apply within session update
Engine --> ReadHistory : one bounded user lookup\nfor new recommendation pages
ReadHistory --> HistoryDatabase
Engine --> Workflow : only when a new batch is needed
Workflow --> UserAdapter : load user preferences
UserAdapter --> Qdrant
Workflow --> Retrieval : retrieve up to 50 candidates
Retrieval --> Adapter : semantic / keyword / hybrid / filters
Adapter --> Qdrant
Workflow --> Ranking : rank candidates
Gateway --> Response : 3. Generate response after commit

note bottom of Session
  InputParser maps intent to SessionRequest inside the lock.
  Registered handlers own actions and pending replies.
  RecommendationPager reuses or refills pages.
  Saved preferences stay separate from searches.
  Preference reports use snapshots without retrieval or AI narration.
  Preference edits replace matching saved opposite tastes.
  Overflow replies preserve preferences and the pending question.
end note
note bottom of Adapter
  Exactly one complete database adapter set is selected.
  Runtime code depends on storage interfaces.
  Session storage is separate from catalogue storage.
end note
legend bottom
  Blue: request handling
  Green: fresh recommendation batch
  Yellow: replaceable storage adapters
  AI providers: parser chat, response chat and query embeddings
  Response pages: up to 5 recommendations
  Arrows: calls or data access, not inheritance
endlegend
@enduml
